SC,0009
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1773436905
OL,1,Vk5   ($| ,                      G9/25
OL,2,Vz%k5j5%h7!~sGCONCERN OVER DUBLIN
OL,3,V  z5j5 ju0pGCOURT RULING
OL,5, Labour's Northern Ireland spokesman has
OL,6, said he is disappointed by the Irish
OL,7, Supreme Court's decision to order the
OL,8, release of two convicted terrorists.
OL,10,FKevin McNamara said the decision not to
OL,11,Fsend the men back to the Maze prison in
OL,12,FNorthern Ireland came as a surprise.
OL,14,FIvor Stanbrook, vice chairman of the
OL,15,Fbackbench Conservative Northern Ireland
OL,16,Fcommittee, said the court's decision
OL,17,Fundermined the Anglo-Irish agreement.
OL,19,FThe Northern Ireland office has also
OL,20,Fsaid it is disappointed at the decision
OL,21,Fnot to extradite the two men.
OL,23,T]FFromG13-03-90F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
