OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1773436905
OL,1,Vk5   ($| ,                     G10/25
OL,2,Vz%k5j5%h7!~sGMIXED RESPONSE TO
OL,3,V  z5j5 ju0pGDUBLIN RULING
OL,5, Sinn Fein president Gerry Adams has
OL,6, welcomed the Irish Supreme Court ruling
OL,7, not to extradite two convicted
OL,8, terrorists to Northern Ireland.
OL,10,FThe ruling showed that the British
OL,11,Flegal, judicial and penal system was
OL,12,F"corrupt and racist" said Mr Adams.
OL,14,FHowever, Democratic Unionist leader Rev
OL,15,FIan Paisley said the Irish courts were
OL,16,F"prejudiced in favour of the IRA and
OL,17,Fmurderers and terrorists".
OL,19,FAlan Dukes, Fine Gael leader in the
OL,20,FIrish Republic, also criticised the
OL,21,Fdecision as a "kind of nonsense".
OL,23,T]FFromG13-03-90F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49611
SC,0011
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1773436905
OL,1,Vk5   ($| ,                     G11/25
OL,2,Vz%k5j5%h7!~sGUNIONISTS ATTACK
OL,3,V  z5j5 ju0pGCOURT DECISION
OL,5, An Ulster Unionist MP has attacked the
OL,6, Dublin court ruling not to send back
OL,7, two convicted terrorists to the Maze
OL,8, prison in Northern Ireland.
OL,10,FKen Maginnis, the Ulster Unionist
OL,11,Fsecurity spokesman, described the
OL,12,Fgrounds on which the men were released
OL,13,Fas an "absolute nonsense".
OL,15,FThe Dublin Supreme Court said Dermot
OL,16,FFinucane and James Pius Clarke faced
OL,17,Fthe risk of assault from prison
OL,18,Fofficers if returned to the Maze jail.
OL,20,FMr Maginnis said the ruling could mean
OL,21,Fthe end of the Anglo-Irish agreement.
OL,23,T]FFromG13-03-90F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
