OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGKINNOCK AWARDED
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGLIBEL DAMAGES
OL,4,D
OL,5, Labour leader Neil Kinnock has received
OL,6, "very substantial" libel damages over a
OL,7, newspaper claim about a family holiday.
OL,9,FThe Sun and News of the World
OL,10,Fnewspapers had alleged in 1987 that
OL,11,FMr Kinnock jumped a queue to book
OL,12,Finto a holiday apartment in Corfu.
OL,14,FCounsel for the papers apologised for
OL,15,Fcausing a "disturbance to his family
OL,16,Fholiday" and for publishing allegations
OL,17,F"which they accept were untrue".
OL,19,FCounsel for Mr Kinnock said the papers
OL,20,Fhad alleged he used his political
OL,21,Fposition to take precedence over others
OL,23,T]FFromG13-03-90F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
